{%- doc -%}
  The opening of "The Zinara Difference" table - Figma 7930:96294: the frame,
  heading and column names. Each "Difference row" block renders one row
  (pdp-difference-row) and the section closes the table after the last.
  Echoed as strings because the elements are closed elsewhere.

  The heading mixes two colours mid-sentence ("The *Zinara* Difference"), so
  the accented run is marked with [brackets] in the setting and swapped for a
  span here - a second text setting would let the two halves drift apart.

  @param {object} labels - the product section's settings
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign heading_html = labels.difference_heading | replace: '[', '<span class="pdp_difference_title_accent">' | replace: ']', '</span>'
  echo '<section class="pdp_difference" data-animate data-animate-from="scale">'
  echo '<h2 class="pdp_difference_title">'
  echo heading_html
  echo '</h2><table class="pdp_difference_table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">'
  echo labels.difference_col_feature | default: 'Feature' | escape
  echo '</th><th scope="col">'
  echo labels.difference_col_ours | default: 'Zinara' | escape
  echo '</th><th scope="col">'
  echo labels.difference_col_others | default: 'Typical Brands' | escape
  echo '</th></tr></thead><tbody>'
-%}
